=== Walled Town ===

start:
You approach the imposing stone walls of a fortified town. A stern guard stands at the gate, his armor gleaming in the sunlight. He eyes you suspiciously as you approach.

Guard: "Halt! This is the walled town of [Town Name]. State your business, traveler. The gates are closed to suspicious folk in these troubled times."

* "[I seek entry to the town.]"
    Guard: "Entry requires a toll of 10 gold pieces, or proof that you're not here to cause trouble. What say you?"
    * "[Pay the toll.]"
        <<changeStat gold, -10>>
        Guard: "Very well. Enter and behave yourself."
        <<stop>>
    * "[I have no gold.]"
        Guard: "Then begone! We don't harbor beggars."
        <<stop>>
    * "[I am on official business.]"
        Guard: "Official business, eh? Prove it or leave."
        <<stop>>
    * "[Never mind.]"
        <<jump leave_alone>>
        Guard: "Suspicious. Very suspicious."
        <<jump refuse_entry>>
        <<stop>>

=== leave_alone ===
You walk away from the gates, the guard's suspicious eyes following you until you disappear from sight.

=== refuse_entry ===
Guard: "I knew it! You're trouble. No entry for the likes of you!"
The guard raises his voice, calling for reinforcements. You should probably leave before this gets worse.

<<end>>    <<stop>>
